From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Keep GSM longword arithmetic at 32 bits on LP64

The GSM arithmetic requires a 32-bit longword. On riscv64, long is 64 bits;
use int, which is 32 bits under the target LP64 ABI. Upstream documents the
same substitution for platforms with 64-bit long in its release notes.

Patch-License: TU-Berlin-2.0
Upstream-Status: Not submitted
Remove-When: Upstream uses fixed-width 32-bit types in a newer release.
---
 inc/private.h | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/inc/private.h b/inc/private.h
--- a/inc/private.h
+++ b/inc/private.h
@@ -18 +18 @@
-typedef long			longword;	/* 32 bit signed int	*/
+typedef int			longword;	/* 32 bit signed int	*/
@@ -21 +21 @@
-typedef unsigned long		ulongword;	/* unsigned longword	*/
+typedef unsigned int		ulongword;	/* unsigned longword	*/
